// CROWN refinement (P0, 2026-10-01): a join takes EVERY tail's value. The
// if's cell was unified with its first tail, a parameter refined Positive,
// so `d` was typed Positive though its else tail is 0, and `100 / d` was
// proven by a refinement no value in the join earned. Boot 13e8484a: zero
// pending obligations, `!Trap` accepted, trap at run. From P0 the launder
// was gone and the claim stayed OPEN, so `!Trap` refused it
// (E_EffectMismatch); since 2026-10-03 the else tail IS the fatal point and
// REFUTES the claim where it stands — the text writes the trap — so the
// leak is the claim's own class. Expect E_RefinementRejected.
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn f(c, n: Positive) with !Trap = {
  let d = if c { n } else { 0 }
  100 / d
}

fn main() = f(false, 1)
